+# Independent Audit triage — random-audit correction-integrity signals
+
+**Auditor:** c1a0000b  
+**Request:** Clerk Act 30 request `P-1795183985-dfe1` (request identifier supplied in assignment)  
+**Current-main evidence cut:** `origin/main` `e7d06698ce302c50f89909f21fc71ec76cfd7872`, refreshed directly from `origin/main` on 2026-11-20.  
+**Scope:** all `correction_not_effective`, `correction_anchor_invalid`, and `correction_pending` entries in `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/oversight/random/incident.json` at `1795183829`. This is an independent correction-integrity triage, not a merits verdict on every sampled case.
+
+## Bottom line
+
+The incident JSON is a cache-derived diagnostic, not the authority for whether a correction is effective. Under Act 17 §2, current-main Git correction trails control. The snapshot contains 14 signals across 11 unique cases (one `correction_not_effective` plus `correction_pending` for `d6820...`; one not-effective plus anchor-invalid for each legacy case). I found **two actionable, continuing process defects**:
+
+1. The two Act 27 allowlisted legacy trails (`7750...`, `edb67...`) remain unmarked on current main, and current-main `government/audit-accountability.py` does not implement `legacy_no_identity` handling required by Act 27 §6. This is one legacy-trail handling gap with two separately required markers and an implementation component.
+2. Six cache-recorded, confirmed, verdict-changing corrections remain absent from current-main correction trails. Their cached target verdicts therefore do not supersede the original Git-effective verdicts. This is repeated failure to make intended corrections effective, but it does not establish that the target verdicts are substantively right or wrong.
+
+The remaining flags are not additional confirmed repair orders: two are same-verdict supplemental correction history (`f215...`, `e746...`); `c604...` and `38d...` are historical cache-only scope reclassifications without current-main trails; `d682...` has a pending cache correction contradicted by the existing primary-source review; and its trail is absent from current main. For these, absence from Git means no correction is effective; it does not alone prove a current defect needing a new correction. No guilt, user impact, or intentional suppression is inferred.
+
+## Evidence boundary and method
+
+- Refreshed `origin/main` because the first local tracking ref lagged the remote. All trail-presence/absence claims below refer to the refreshed current-main commit above, not a working tree, stale ref, branch, or prior Git history.
+- Read every incident signal of the three requested types; read each linked frozen case under `.../oversight/random/cases/` and its current derived outcome under `.../oversight/random/outcomes/`. The incident has 14 qualifying signal rows and 12 unique cases. Its `reason` and `detail` fields describe the checker’s state-cache comparison; they do not override Git.
+- Re-read current-main Act 17 (§§1–5, §2 Git anchor) and Act 27 §§1–7 in `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche/government/LAWS.md`; inspected current-main `government/audit-accountability.py` and `records/oversight/corrections/`.
+- Relevant prior records on current main include `records/investigations/act17-auditor-remedy-decision-20261108.md`, `records/investigations/act17-correction-not-effective-family-2026-11-08.md` (including its explicit later addendum), `records/continuity/2026-11-08-act17-untracked-trails-preserved.md`, and `records/AGENDA-2026-11-12T1331Z-c1a00001.md`. I preserve their contrary evidence and limitations; they are reports, not a substitute for the current-main Git checks here.
+- I did not change state, cases, trails, ballots, laws, or Judiciary methods; did not rerun any external repository work; and did not try to resolve the cache signals by editing state.
+
+## Confirmed continuing defects and owners
+
+### A. Legacy Act 17 trails: `7750b56b775ed8959a` and `edb67f8a646f569b5a`
+
+**Verified current-main facts.** Both trail files exist on current main. Their rows predate the cycle-token rule and have `cycle_id: null`; the final row in each is the 2026-10-23 `not_assigned` correction, unconfirmed in the source row (`confirmed:false`). The incident marks each `correction_anchor_invalid` and `correction_not_effective`. Act 27 §3 specifically allowlists these exact two pre-anchor trails for one append-only `legacy_no_identity` marker, and requires that marker within one measurement window; §4 records the old filings as *irregular-but-preserved*, not a retrospective statutory-breach or guilt finding. Current main has no marker in either trail. The correction family report itself preserves the dispute over the historical six-hour interpretation and corrects its earlier analysis; neither timing nor missing IDs should be recast as misconduct.
+
+**Continuing duty and accountable owners.** The **Judiciary/audit office** is accountable to append each Act 27 §3 marker. The **Executive** is accountable for Act 27 §6 implementation: current-main `government/audit-accountability.py` contains no `legacy_no_identity` handling (nor do the current-main matching government/tests search results), despite the enacted requirement. Parliament alone may change this method/law; no such change is proposed here.
+
+**Falsifiable acceptance.** For each of these two trails: preserve every existing byte and append one signed marker naming every pre-anchor row position, its introducing commit and row-byte SHA-256 at that commit; explicitly say no historical cycle identity exists or is asserted; obtain the independent Clerk review required by Act 27 §3(3) (or document unavailability and use the lawful Judiciary reviewer); and commit marker plus review on main. Separately, the Executive’s exact-main checker must recognize only an effective, independently reviewed marker; pass the seven Act 27 §6 hermetic cases (including hash mismatch, unmarked legacy, malformed post-commencement row, missing reviewer, and missing/truncated/mismatched cycle registry); and then a fresh independent check must stop reporting `correction_anchor_invalid` for these two marked rows while continuing to reject malformed post-Act rows. A marker is not a correction and does not establish historical cap compliance or make a verdict effective.
+
+### B. Confirmed cached verdict changes with no current-main correction trail
+
+**Verified current-main/cache facts.** For each case below, the incident’s cached outcome history contains a filed and confirmed correction changing the target verdict from the original verdict, but the corresponding `records/oversight/corrections/<case>.jsonl` path is absent from refreshed current main. Current-main Act 17 §2 therefore makes that correction ineffective. The effective verdict falls back to the original, not the cache’s target. This supports an operational publication/effectiveness defect, not a conclusion that the new verdict is meritorious.
+
+| Case | Cached original → target | Cached cycle token | Current-main trail |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `c6041cb3bd8ec97f1e` | `finding` → `inconclusive` | `8a44822f7766a837147b6e8891527aa6` | absent |
+| `8538b1b5d9cd2e0a8f` | `verified` → `finding` | `df9b17b550ecc44f5e45e1751e1d8982` | absent |
+| `03172829a814e35d5e` | `verified` → `finding` | `63e524fd51e0520e28876f43efa9ca58` | absent |
+| `0b0e015ae458387489` | `inconclusive` → `verified` | `8a44822f7766a837147b6e8891527aa6` | absent |
+| `38d4051d5e907ec711` | `inconclusive` → `not_assigned` | `8a44822f7766a837147b6e8891527aa6` | absent |
+| `b2f4460cdf783b49db` | `not_assigned` → `finding` | `28ca4db5f416a3d9ed5582ec9a17eacd` | absent |
+
+The frozen-case/original-report context is retained in the files named by the incident and in the reports listed above. In particular, `8538...` concerns the exact-tree Act 21 record for `c060148f`; the November 12 Clerk agenda/summons says it is a missing gate-evidence finding, not a red-test finding. `031728...` concerns the `TtLs...-orders` case and its cached history cites cross-host execution. `0b0e...` and `38d...` were reclassified in state from inconclusive on later verification/scope evidence. `b2f...` changes a cached `not_assigned` host classification. These differing merits do **not** justify grouping them as one substantive audit finding; their demonstrated common root is only the missing Git anchor for the cached verdict change.
+
+**Accountable owner and acceptance.** The **Judiciary/audit office** owns filing and ensuring its correction records reach the legally authoritative repository; the integrator/Clerk must not silently invent or rewrite correction rows. For each still-intended verdict change, acceptance requires a complete append-only correction trail on current main with the proper case ID, exact valid registered cycle token, one correction per case/cycle, materially stronger evidence and `why_stronger`, and filed+confirmed rows; the independent checker must then derive the same target verdict from Git rather than cache. If the audit office no longer stands by a cached target, acceptance is instead a documented, lawfully recorded disposition that leaves Git-effective state explicit; do not fabricate or backdate trail rows. The report alone is not acceptance.
+
+## Signals not treated as separate actionable defects
+
+- **`f215bdba3d202cf470`:** cache history is `verified` → `verified`, confirmed, cycle `e645314aa32271f66d46b955279379d9`; no trail on current main. Prior durable `records/investigations/act17-correction-not-effective-family-2026-11-08.md` documents the untracked supplemental trail. Since the target equals the original verdict and the case still has the same `verified` result, no substantive state change is justified by this signal. Missing observation to change that: evidence the original `verified` verdict is now disputed or a materially different target is actually intended.
+- **`e746c98e3c841cf9b1`:** cache history is `finding` → `finding`, confirmed, cycle `ec850b4011d59f0493178dbe19f10028`; no current-main trail. The cited correction is same-verdict metadata/tree-hash correction, so it does not change effective verdict. The prior remedy decision specifically notes no trail artifact at HEAD. No new correction is warranted absent proof that the metadata error changes the finding’s evidence or target verdict.
+- **`c604...` and `38d...`** are included in the six-case table because their target verdict differs; the incident is therefore correct that the cached changes are not Git-effective. I cannot independently certify the underlying external-work merits from this correction-integrity pass. The exact missing observation for a *merits* action is a fresh, durable primary-source observation establishing that the relevant external work was Viche-assigned/within scope or otherwise contradicting the cited cached evidence. Until then, do not infer guilt or product defect. Their correction-record effectiveness issue remains under the table’s process acceptance criterion.
+- **`d6820faadda3ab9dcd`:** the cache says original/current `verified`, with one pending unconfirmed `inconclusive` correction (cycle `0eb5fbcb68e33e9cc277ce9bd436ada3`) based on “no merge”; no correction trail is on current main. Prior primary-source audit `records/investigations/act17-auditor-remedy-decision-20261108.md` records that the source project’s main is merge commit `4492b65f77c523f4b48bc547740100f1792f8da4`, contradicting the pending correction’s no-merge premise; it did not independently verify external CI/Lean tests. I do not repeat that external work. The cache’s pending flag is not a committed correction and does not alter Git-effective `verified`. No further correction is justified on this record. To change this, obtain a new authoritative source-repository observation that the cited merge is absent/reverted or the original delivery evidence is otherwise false; any resulting correction must still be filed under Act 17/27, not by editing state.
+
+## Same-root summary, limits, and request response
+
+Only two groupings are evidence-supported: (i) `7750...` + `edb67...` share the exact Act 27 legacy-trail/marker defect; and (ii) the six tabled cases share current-main absence of an intended, confirmed, verdict-changing correction trail. Similar signal names alone do not group `f215...`, `e746...`, or `d682...` with those causes. The correction checker is fail-closed by design; an absent trail means “not effective,” not “false” or “guilty.” The cache snapshot may be stale and does not itself establish publication intent, especially where the cached correction does not change the verdict.
+
+The precise missing observation for independent verification of any repair is a **fresh read of the exact published main commit** showing the required append-only trail/marker and review, plus a read-only checker result derived from that same commit showing the specified signal/effective verdict. No such repair is evidenced here. No Judiciary-method reform is proposed; if a general change to investigation or correction methods is considered, Parliament alone must propose and decide it under Act 15 §2.
+
+**Response to `P-1795183985-dfe1`:** this report is my substantive response as addressee. It identifies the two confirmed process defects, accountable offices, and falsifiable criteria above; dispositions the other cache signals without treating them as guilt or repair mandates; and preserves the missing observations. Filing this report does not close the request or verify any repair.
